Subject: Make setup-pstack detect models and write its rule for Claude Code
Kind: claudify

Claude Code has no models API, so setup-pstack reads the Agent tool's
`model` and `effort` values and treats each pair as a slug. Claude Code
loads every `~/.claude/rules/*.md` file into each session and needs no
frontmatter, so the Cursor `alwaysApply` header goes. Fast slugs and
Gemini's ceiling do not exist here, so the budget ladder only moves the
last token. Older rules from this build hold Sonnet where upstream held
Grok and never had a `# defaults: 2` form, so the migration step looks
for `sonnet-*` and drops the Gemini pool case. The judge pool is checked
by model, since every model here is one vendor. The rule's comments say
how a value maps onto the Agent tool, since every session loads them.

